with machine learning models.\n\n4. **Qdrant**: This open-source vector search engine is built for RAG applications, focusing on speed and memory efficiency. It offers a free tier for small-scale usage.\n\n5. **Chroma**: A newer entry in the vector database space, Chroma is designed for ease of use and integration with various machine learning frameworks.\n\n6. **Vespa**: While more complex to set up, Vespa is a powerful option for applications that require advanced search capabilities alongside vector storage.\n\n7. **pgvector**: An extension for PostgreSQL, pgvector allows users to store and query vector embeddings directly within a relational database, making it a good option for those already using PostgreSQL.\n\n8. **Redis and MongoDB**: These NoSQL databases also offer vector support, providing flexibility for applications that require both traditional and vector-based querying.\n\n### Factors to Consider When Choosing a Vector Database\n\nWhen selecting a vector database for RAG, consider the following factors:\n\n- **Scalability**: Ensure the database can handle your expected data volume and query load.\n- **Integration**: Look for compatibility with existing systems and frameworks you are using.\n- **Performance**: Evaluate the database's speed in processing queries and its ability to handle high-dimensional vectors efficiently.\n- **Cost**: Consider the pricing model, especially if you expect to scale your application.\n- **Ease of Use**: Some databases may require more setup and maintenance than others, impacting your development timeline.\n\n### Conclusion\n\nThe effectiveness of a RAG model is intrinsically linked to the performance of the vector database used. Popular choices like Pinecone, Milvus, and Weaviate offer various features that cater to different needs, from ease of use to high scalability. By carefully evaluating your specific requirements, you can select the most suitable vector database to enhance your RAG applications.", 'isUser': False, 'timestamp': '2025-11-07T13:18:56.550Z', 'retrieved': [{'index': 1, 'type': 'text', 'content': 'What is RAG? -> Retrieval-Augmented Generation = vector search + LLM generation.', 'snippet': 'What is RAG? -> Retrieval-Augmented Generation = vector search + LLM generation.', 'distance': 0.6236, 'metadata': {'source': 'ml_llm_interview_cheat_sheet.pdf', 'page': 'N/A', 'table_index': None, 'image_index': None}}, {'index': 2, 'type': 'text', 'content': 'RAG with ChromaDB', 'snippet': 'RAG with ChromaDB', 'distance': 1.1209, 'metadata': {'source': 'ml_llm_interview_cheat_sheet.pdf', 'page': 'N/A', 'table_index': None, 'image_index': None}}, {'index': 3, 'type': 'text', 'content': 'BM25 vs Vector search? -> BM25 = keywords; Vector = semantics; hybrid improves precision+recall.', 'snippet': 'BM25 vs Vector search? -> BM25 = keywords; Vector = semantics; hybrid improves precision+recall.', 'distance': 1.2916, 'metadata': {'source': 'ml_llm_interview_cheat_sheet.pdf', 'page': 'N/A', 'table_index': None, 'image_index': None}}, {'index': 4, 'type': 'text', 'content': 'Memory mgmt? -> Conversation buffer + vector memory to persist context.', 'snippet': 'Memory mgmt? -> Conversation buffer + vector memory to persist context.', 'distance': 1.5801, 'metadata': {'source': 'ml_llm_interview_cheat_sheet.pdf', 'page': 'N/A', 'table_index': None, 'image_index': None}}, {'index': 5, 'type': 'text', 'content': 'spectrogram-like ECG data.', 'snippet': 'spectrogram-like ECG data.', 'distance': 1.5486, 'metadata': {'source': 'ml_llm_interview_cheat_sheet.pdf', 'page': 'N/A', 'table_index': None, 'image_index': None}}, {'index': 6, 'type': 'text', 'content': 'Metrics? -> Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1-score (important for imbalance).', 'snippet': 'Metrics? -> Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1-score (important for imbalance).', 'distance': 1.4132, 'metadata': {'source': 'ml_llm_interview_cheat_sheet.pdf', 'page': 'N/A', 'table_index': None, 'image_index': None}}]}]
